<title>USA: Case buys agricultural software company.</title>
<headline>Case buys agricultural software company.</headline>
<dateline>RACINE, Wis. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Case Corp said Friday it acquired Agri-Logic, a developer of software for agricultural applications, from  Fluid Power Industries.</p>
<p>Terms of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Agri-Logic, based in Brazil, Indiana, provides computer software for precision or site-specific farming. Products include software for making yield maps and for surveying.</p>
<p>Case said the acquisition will enhance its Advanced Farming Systems line of products.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
